From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cts: stop on a clock pin off its hierarchical net

With OPENROAD_HIERARCHICAL=1, CTS could connect a clock pin to the flat
net only (OpenROAD#11718, #11719). The session that ran CTS times it;
every stage that reads 4_1_cts.odb back builds the hierarchical view,
where the pin is undriven and what it clocks is unclocked: 258 to 6,830
register pins on each of XiangShan's blocks, found only by check_setup
on the read-back database. The CTS stage now stops before writing the
database when a clock net has a hierarchical net and pins on none.

Not upstreamed. Retires when OpenROAD#11718 and #11719 are in and the
check has been upstreamed or found unneeded.

---
diff --git a/flow/scripts/cts.tcl b/flow/scripts/cts.tcl
--- a/flow/scripts/cts.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/cts.tcl
@@ -86,5 +86,12 @@ report_metrics 4 "cts final"
 
 source_step_tcl POST CTS
 
+# A clock pin left off its hierarchical net is undriven once the
+# database is read back, and every register behind it unclocked in each
+# later stage, though this session still times it.
+if { $::env(OPENROAD_HIERARCHICAL) } {
+  check_hier_clock_nets
+}
+
 orfs_write_db $::env(RESULTS_DIR)/4_1_cts.odb
 orfs_write_sdc $::env(RESULTS_DIR)/4_cts.sdc
diff --git a/flow/scripts/util.tcl b/flow/scripts/util.tcl
--- a/flow/scripts/util.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/util.tcl
@@ -226,6 +226,34 @@ proc source_env_var_if_exists { env_var } {
 }
 
 
+# Stops on a clock net that has a hierarchical net and pins that are on
+# none: the hierarchical view, which a stage reading the database back
+# times, leaves those pins undriven.
+proc check_hier_clock_nets { } {
+  set off {}
+  foreach net [[ord::get_db_block] getNets] {
+    if { [$net getSigType] != "CLOCK" } {
+      continue
+    }
+    set on_hier_net 0
+    set flat_only {}
+    foreach iterm [$net getITerms] {
+      if { [$iterm getModNet] == "NULL" } {
+        lappend flat_only [$iterm getName]
+      } else {
+        set on_hier_net 1
+      }
+    }
+    if { $on_hier_net } {
+      lappend off {*}$flat_only
+    }
+  }
+  if { [llength $off] > 0 } {
+    error "[llength $off] clock pins are off their hierarchical net,\
+      e.g. [lrange $off 0 4]: read back, what they clock is unclocked."
+  }
+}
+
 # Feature toggle for now, eventually the -hier option
 # will be default and this code will be deleted.
 proc hier_options { } {
